# NFS "silly rename" files: when a file is deleted or replaced while some process
# still holds it open, the NFS client renames it to .nfsXXXXXXXX rather than
# unlinking it, and it lingers until that process exits. Untracked and invisible
# to 'ls', so it is easy to sweep one into a commit with 'git add -A'.
.nfs*

